            "content": [
              {
                "type": "output_text",
                "text": "- **Perseverance hit a major driving milestone: a full “marathon” on Mars.** NASA reported the rover has now driven **26.2 miles (42.195 km)** total on the Martian surface, reaching the mark on **sol 1,890** (about **five years and four months** into the mission). An orbital image from Mars Reconnaissance Orbiter’s **HiRISE** camera also shows the rover and its track marks from above.【5:0†source】\n\n- **Perseverance photographed Earth disappearing behind Mars’s moon Phobos.** In a recent Mastcam-Z image sequence, **Earth appears as a bright point of light** in the Martian sky and is seen **passing behind (being occulted by) Phobos**—a notable skywatching observation from the surface of Mars.【5:1†source】【5:3†source】\n\nIf you tell me whether you want “latest news” as *science results*, *engineering status*, or *new images*, I can summarize only that category.",
